# Headings

Use headings to show the structure of a dashboard or page. Choose each level for the structure, not for the size you want. Screen reader users move around a page by its headings.

## Heading levels

Use one main heading on a page, and keep heading levels in order. Do not skip a level. If a heading looks too big, give it a different size. Do not change its level.

Write headings in sentence case, such as “Living room lights”. Do not write a whole heading in capitals. [Write clear titles](../content/writing-guidelines/clear-titles.html) explains how to word them.

## A reading is not a heading

A large reading, such as “21°C”, is a value, not a heading. Do not mark it up as a heading to make it bigger. Do not make a paragraph look like a heading while leaving it as a paragraph.

